---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Comments from '../../../components/Comments.astro';

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Looking for a Website? Get Back to Your Calling - Caleb McGennis"
  description="You didn't start a church, a practice, or a business to manage a website. Why we started Bearded Digital, what it takes off your plate, what it costs, and how to know if it's a fit."
  type="article"
  publishedTime="2026-11-23"
  author="Caleb Michael McGennis"
  image="/images/social/get-back-to-your-calling-bearded-digital-og.jpg"
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="bg-soho-white py-20 md:py-32 px-4 border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <a href="/blog/entrepreneur-ai" class="inline-flex items-center text-mcgennis-navy hover:text-mcgennis-gold transition-colors mb-8">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to An Entrepreneur in a World of AI
      </a>
      <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-display font-bold mb-8 text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">
        Looking for a Website? Get Back to Your Calling
      </h1>
      <div class="h-1 w-24 bg-brass-horizontal rounded-full shadow-sm mb-8"></div>
      <p class="text-2xl text-gray-500 font-light mb-8">Why we started Bearded Digital, and who it's for.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-gray-500">
        <span>By Caleb Michael McGennis</span>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-23">November 23, 2026</time>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Article Content -->
  <article class="py-16 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl prose prose-lg">
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-8 font-light">
        You didn't start a church, a practice, or a business to manage a website. That one sentence is the whole reason <a href="https://bearded.digital" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-mcgennis-navy hover:text-mcgennis-gold transition-colors underline">Bearded Digital</a> exists.
      </p>

      <figure class="my-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 shadow-sm not-prose">
        <img loading="eager" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" src="/images/bearded-digital/bearded-digital-home.webp" alt="The Bearded Digital home page with the headline Get Back To Your Calling" class="w-full" />
        <figcaption class="p-4 bg-soho-white text-sm text-gray-600 font-light">The first thing you see at bearded.digital</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Full disclosure before anything else: I co-own Bearded Digital with Landen. I handle development and support, and Landen is our developer. So read this knowing I'm biased. I'm going to tell you what we believe, what we do, what it costs, and who we're probably not a fit for.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Why We Exist</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        If you're a pastor, an office manager, or a business owner, the website usually lands on your desk because nobody else will take it. Then it eats your week.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        We don't think that's what you were called to do. Here's how we put it on our site:
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-mcgennis-gold pl-6 my-8 italic text-gray-700">
        &ldquo;You weren't called to fight a website. Every hour you spend fighting a website is an hour taken from the work you were called to. So we take the whole thing. We design it, host it, secure it, keep it current, and make the changes when you ask.&rdquo;
      </blockquote>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        That's the mission in plain English: <strong>we run your website so you can get back to your calling.</strong> Your work matters. Focus on it while we partner with you on your website.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Who It's For</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        We built Bearded Digital for churches, ministries, practices, and small businesses, and especially for the ones without a tech person. One of the questions on our FAQ is &ldquo;What if we don't have a tech person?&rdquo; The answer is: &ldquo;Good. That is exactly who we built this for.&rdquo;
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Some of the sites we've launched include LifePointe Church in Fulton, Aviate and the McGennis Group in Jefferson City, Hillbilly Hydration in Mid-Missouri, Binnacle Mitigation in Kirksville, and Caleb Steffen, MD in Jefferson City. You can see them in the <a href="https://bearded.digital/#work" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-mcgennis-navy hover:text-mcgennis-gold transition-colors underline">work section</a> of our site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">What We Take Off Your Plate</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The idea is that you never log in again. Every plan covers:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 text-gray-600 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Custom design.</strong> Built for your church, practice, or business.</li>
        <li><strong>Managed hosting, security, and daily backups.</strong> We host it, harden it, and back it up every day.</li>
        <li><strong>Updates and edits.</strong> You send the change and we make it, on a response time you can count on.</li>
        <li><strong>A site people can use.</strong> Mobile-first and fast, so people find what they came for.</li>
        <li><strong>Getting found.</strong> Technical SEO, sitemaps, Search Console, local listings, and analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>A person who answers.</strong> When something's wrong, you tell a human in Missouri.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        We connect the booking, payment, CRM, and media tools you already use. No new logins, and no training day for your team. If you want help reaching more of the right people, we do Google Ads, social media, SEO content, landing pages, and branding refreshes too.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        And it stays yours. It's your site and your domain. You keep your email, and we change records, not owners. In our words: &ldquo;You own the site. We're just managers.&rdquo;
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">How It Works</h2>

      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 mb-6 text-gray-600 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Kickoff.</strong> A short intake and access to your current site. That's most of what we need from you.</li>
        <li><strong>Build.</strong> We build the new site, harden the security, and turn on backups.</li>
        <li><strong>Content.</strong> We move your content over, test everything, and refine the design until it sounds like you.</li>
        <li><strong>Review.</strong> You look it over and tell us what to change. We work the list until you're happy.</li>
        <li><strong>Go live.</strong> We launch it, submit the sitemap, and connect analytics and search. You go back to work.</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        After launch, the hosting, security, backups, updates, and edits keep going every month. That's the part most people never want to think about again.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">What It Costs</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        There's no design fee. Other agencies charge $2,000 to $5,000 up front. With us you pay the first month and we start. Here are the plans as of this writing:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 text-gray-600 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Basic, $129/month</strong> ($100/month paid annually): up to 5 pages, 1 hour of edits a month, 72-hour response time.</li>
        <li><strong>Grow, $279/month</strong> ($250/month paid annually): up to 10 pages, 2 hours of edits a month, priority support, 24&ndash;48-hour response time.</li>
        <li><strong>Pro, $479/month</strong> ($450/month paid annually): unlimited pages and edits, local SEO, cPanel access, 24-hour response time.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Plans run 12 months, then go month-to-month. Emergencies jump the queue on every plan. Custom features are scoped separately. The current numbers are always on the <a href="https://bearded.digital/#pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-mcgennis-navy hover:text-mcgennis-gold transition-colors underline">pricing section</a> of our site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Is It the Right Fit?</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Honestly, maybe not. We say this on our own site: &ldquo;We're not the cheapest option. Doing it yourself is cheaper, and you pay for it in time.&rdquo; If you enjoy building your own site and have the hours for it, you should do that.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        We're a fit if you'd rather hand the whole thing to someone in Missouri who takes it over completely, speaks plain English, and answers when you call.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900 tracking-tight">What Clients Say</h2>

      <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-mcgennis-gold pl-6 my-8 italic text-gray-700">
        &ldquo;Awesome company to work with! Bearded Digital exceeded our expectations: creative design, quick response time, and functionalities beyond our request. They turned our vision into reality!&rdquo;
        <span class="block not-italic text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Angie Abbott, Reign Ministries</span>
      </blockquote>

      <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-mcgennis-gold pl-6 my-8 italic text-gray-700">
        &ldquo;The team at Bearded was personable and easy to work with. Got the job done without the headache and valued our input the entire process. Would suggest them to anyone!&rdquo;
        <span class="block not-italic text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Phillip Rutledge, Hillbilly Hydration</span>
      </blockquote>

      <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-mcgennis-gold pl-6 my-8 italic text-gray-700">
        &ldquo;Everyone I've worked with at Bearded.Digital is top notch professionals. They take my small ideas and turn them into great projects. Very happy, highly recommend!&rdquo;
        <span class="block not-italic text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Kelli Hart, Revival IV Hydration</span>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="bg-mcgennis-navy text-white rounded-xl p-8 my-12 not-prose">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold mb-4 tracking-tight">Start With a Free Plan</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
          Put your website address into the <a href="https://bearded.digital/plan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline hover:text-mcgennis-gold">free plan tool</a>. In about a minute it shows your platform, your speed, what we'd fix, and a price. No email needed.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
          No website yet? <a href="https://bearded.digital/?source=new-website#contact" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline hover:text-mcgennis-gold">Let's talk about a new one</a>, or call (417) 893-0298.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Comments />

  <section class="py-16 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto text-center">
      <a href="/blog/entrepreneur-ai" class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 rounded-xl border border-gray-300 text-gray-700 font-medium tracking-wide hover:border-mcgennis-navy hover:text-mcgennis-navy transition-all duration-300">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to An Entrepreneur in a World of AI
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
